Instruction cache flood
=======================

Part of HW_Specific: tests that stress one hardware resource, to study how
interference on it shows up in other partitions. The sizes come from
BENCH_TOOLS/arch_config.h (cache and TLB geometry of the target).

What it tests
-------------

Interference caused by filling the instruction cache.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Every 50 ms executes once a block of code as big as the L1 instruction cache
(32 KB): a chain of indirect jumps, generated for each architecture by
BENCH_TOOLS/gen_icache_flooder.c (icache_flood_x86_64.h,
icache_flood_aarch64.h).

Expected output
---------------

"L1 Cache filled 1000 times" every 1000 periods (50 s).

Notes
-----

To change the code size, regenerate the headers, e.g.
    gen_icache_flooder x86_64 32768 icache_flood_x86_64.h
    gen_icache_flooder aarch64 32768 icache_flood_aarch64.h

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/CACHES/ICACHE_PRIVATE/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/CACHES/ICACHE_PRIVATE/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
